  "raw_text": "148\n\nMâ kâkan\n \n–\n \ntoasted grain\n \n/ grano tostado\n\nMâ krikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto harvest, to reap\n \n/ cosechar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nInsla krikaia, Insla dâkaia, Dâkaia\n)\n\nMâ sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto bear fruit, to produce fruit, to get results, to succeed\n \n/ dar fruto, producir fruto, obtener\nresultados, tener éxito\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-11\n):\n \nBan kra karna trai munaia sma, sakuna mâ yamni sâkma\n \n–\n \nMaybe you will (have to) try hard, but you will\nget good results\n \n/ Tal vez (tendrá que) esforzarse mucho, pero obtendrá buenos resultados)\n\nMâ tawahkia\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfirstfruits\n \n/ primicias\n\nPas mâ nani\n \n–\n \nfirstfruits\n \n/ primeros frutos\n\nPlun mâ\n \n–\n \nfruit, grain\n \n/ fruta, grano\n\nSpirit mâ\n \n–\n \nfruitage of the spirit\n \n/ fruto del espíritu\n\nMabiara\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nLal mabiara\n \nAre there other common usages of this word?\n\nMadakura\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nMâ dakura\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npond, pool, lake, lagoon\n \n/ estanque, piscina, lago, laguna\n \n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner también:\n\nLakun\n)\n\nMadiskaia\n \n(\ndbta,dba,db,lrw,dict,dictu,bh,sn\n;\n \nMâ diskaia\n,\nDiskaia\n-dict-alt,dictu-alt\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto shade, to overshadow\n \n/\nsombrear, eclipsar\n\nMamdiskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto shade you, to overshadow you\n \n/ sombrearte, eclipsarlo\n\nMagia\n \n(\nlfb\n-\nSpanish word\n \n/ palabra española\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmagic\n\nMago\n \n(\nlfb\n-\nSpanish word\n \n/ palabra española\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmagician\n\n(Construct form:\n \nMagoka\n)\n\nMahbra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \negg, ...\n \n/ huevo,\n \n…\n\nKalila mahbra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nchicken egg\n \n/ huevo de gallina\n\nMahka\n \n(adv\n-\n1)\n \n–\n \nnow, at once\n, immediately\n \n/ ahora, a la vez, inmediatamente\n \n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nAihni\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nMahka waia\n \n–\n \nlet’s go\n \n/ vamos\n;\n \nLit\n:\n \nWe must go now\n \n/\n \nD\nebemos irnos\n \nahora\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nMahka auna\n \n–\n \nI’m going right now\n \n/ Voy ahora\n)\n\nMahka alki daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto apply immediately, to put into practice immediately\n \n/ aplicar de inmediato, poner en\n\npráctica de inmediato\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n12/18\n):\n \nSaulo witin\n \ndîa lan\n \ntakan ba\n \nmahka alki daukan.\n \n–\n \nWhat Saul learned, he put into practice right away.\n\n/ Lo que Saúl aprendió, lo puso en práctica de inmediato.)\n\nMahka\n \n(adv\n-\n2)\n \n–\n \nalready\n \n/ ya\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nMahka wan\n \n–\n \nalready went\n \n/ ya se fue\n)\n\nMahsis\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nunfruitful,\n \nsterile (agriculture)\n \n/\n \ninfructífera\n, est\né\nril (agricultura)\n\nMahta\n \n–\n \nthe lower part\n \n/ la parte de abajo\n\nPr\nâ\nk mahta\n \n(a/t:\n \nMahta\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nskirt\n \n/ falda\n\nMai\n \n–\n \nyou, to you, your\n \n/ tu, para ti\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nMai\n \ncan be put in the middle of a compound verb to indicate that the object of that verb is\n \nyou\n.\n \nEx/Ej:\n \nKunin mai\n\nmunri\n \n–\n \nI tricked you\n \n/\n \nMai\n \nse puede poner en el medio de un verbo compuesto para indicar que el objeto de ese verbo eres\n \ntú\n.\n\nEx/Ej:\n \nKunin mai munri\n \n–\n \nTe engañé\n)\n\nMaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give you, to allow you, to cause you\n \n/ darte, permitirte, hacerte\n \n(irregularity of / irregularidad\nde:\n \nYabaia\n \n–\n \nto give\n \n/ dar. See also/ Ver también:\n \nAikaia\n \n&\n \nWankaia\n)\n \n(See entry below/ver entrada debajo:\n\nMaikaia\n)\n\nMaia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nMaya\n\nMaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give you, to allow you, to cause you\n \n/ darte, permitirte, hacerte\n \n(irregularity of / irregularidad de:\n\nYabaia\n \n–\n \nto give\n \n/ dar. See also/ Ver también:\n \nAikaia\n \n&\n \nWankaia\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej-Present tense/Tiempo presente:\n \nYang maikisna\n \n–\n \nI give you\n \n/ Te doy;\n \nMan maikisma\n \n–\n \nYou give yourself\n \n/ Te das;\n \nWitin\nmaikisa\n \n–\n \nHe/she gives you\n \n/ Él/ella te da)\n\n(Ex/Ej-Past tense/Tiempo pasado:\n \nYang maikri\n \n–\n \nI gave you\n \n/ Te di;\n \nMan maikram\n \n–\n \nYou gave yourself\n \n/ Te diste;\n \nWitin maikan\n \n–\n\nHe/she gave you\n \n/\n \nÉl/ella te\n \ndio)\n\n(Ex/Ej- Future tense/Tiempo futuro:\n \nYang maikamna\n \n–\n \nI will give you\n \n/ Te daré;\n \nMan maikma\n \n–\n \nYou will give yourself\n \n/ Te darás;\n\nWitin maikbia\n \n–\n \nHe/she will give you\n \n/\n \nÉl/ella\n \nte dará)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-15\n):\n \nJehova ra makas spirit holikira maikbia\n \n–\n \nBeg Jehovah to give you holy spirit\n \n/ Ruego a Jehová que te dé espíritu\nsanto)",
